@startuml
title P1 Telegram / App Parity - Deploy, Use and Rollback

actor Operator
participant Coordinator
participant "Telegram adapter" as Bot
participant "App surfaces" as App
participant "Common media / transmission / policy" as Core
participant Nodes

== Deploy ==
Operator -> Operator : record artifacts + SQLite-safe backup
Operator -> Coordinator : deploy additive coordinator first
Coordinator -> Core : install / reconcile additive state
Operator -> Nodes : deploy capability-honest clients
Nodes -> Coordinator : register exact replacement capability set
Operator -> App : expose read-only history / presence
Operator -> App : expose mutations after redaction checks
Operator -> Bot : expose attachments / callbacks last

== Runtime ==
Bot -> Core : SubmitMedia with verified Telegram ActorContext
Core --> Bot : ready / exact common failure
Bot -> Core : commit immediate voice after_current default
Bot --> Bot : deliver keyboard asynchronously
alt authorized callback before start
  Bot -> Core : atomic cancel default + create replacement
else start wins or callback invalid
  Core --> Bot : too_late / expired / forbidden; no mutation
end
Core --> App : sanitized history / presence / policy result

== Drain-first rollback ==
Operator -> Bot : withdraw new media / inline dispatch
Operator -> App : withdraw new mutations; keep reads / cancel
Operator -> Core : canonical cancel and bounded drain
Operator -> Coordinator : stop sole writer + checkpoint
Operator -> Coordinator : deploy immediate predecessor
note right of Coordinator
  Preserve additive tables.
  Keep new surfaces withdrawn.
  Legacy voice remains supported.
end note

@enduml
